+# Working with Rojo
+
+Git is the source of truth for this game. Code lives in files under `src/`, and `rojo serve`
+syncs those files into your own dev place in Studio. Studio is where you run, test, and playtest.
+You don't author code there. The README's Layout table shows where each folder lands in the place.
+
+## Setup
+
+1. Install the tools with `rokit install`. It reads `rokit.toml`, which pins `rojo`, `pesde`,
+   `luau-lsp`, `selene`, and `stylua`. Run `rojo --version` and make sure it is the pinned
+   version. A second `rojo` on your PATH leads to protocol-version errors in the plugin.
+2. Install packages: `pesde install` in the repo root, then the same in `test_packages/`. This
+   fills `roblox_packages/` (game packages) and `test_packages/roblox_packages/` (Jest).
+3. Create your own dev place, published under your account or group, and add its place id to
+   `servePlaceIds` in `default.project.json`. Rojo then refuses to live-sync into any other place,
+   so a stray Connect can't overwrite a shared place.
+4. Run `rojo serve`. It listens on port 34872 (`servePort`). In Studio, open your dev place and
+   click **Connect** in the Rojo plugin.
+
+## Where to make changes
+
+- **Every change goes in a file.** Edit scripts in your editor, not in Studio. The next sync
+  overwrites a script edited in Studio, and Git never sees that edit.
+- Script types come from file names: `Foo.server.luau` is a Script, `Foo.client.luau` is a
+  LocalScript, and any other `.luau` file is a ModuleScript. Put attributes and tags in a
+  `Foo.meta.json` beside the file.
+- Specs go in `src/ServerScriptService/Tests/Specs` as `Name.spec.luau`.
+- Treat installed packages (`roblox_packages/`, `test_packages/roblox_packages/`) as read-only.
+  The next install replaces them, and the files are hardlinked to a store other projects share.
+  To add or bump a package, edit `pesde.toml`, stop `rojo serve`, run `pesde install`, and
+  commit `pesde.toml` with `pesde.lock`. Require packages through their link
+  (`ReplicatedStorage.Packages.Vide`), never through a `.pesde/...` path.
+- If you build something in Studio that has to be kept (a model, a GUI, a property), export it
+  to its `.rbxm` file or write it into the project file, or the next sync throws it away.
+
+## What to check while serving
+
+- **Is `rojo serve` still running?** Rojo 7.7.x can crash when a file or folder is deleted,
+  moved, or renamed. Studio then quietly stops receiving changes. After any delete, move, or
+  rename, look for `Rojo crashed!` in the terminal. If it crashed, restart `rojo serve` and
+  click Connect again.
+- **Did your edit arrive?** Before you trust a test or playtest, open the script in Studio and
+  check that it has your new code. If an error's line number didn't move with your edit, you're
+  running the old code.
+- **Which checkout is it serving?** The place runs whatever is in the folder `rojo serve`
+  started in, on the branch checked out there. A merged PR changes nothing in that folder until
+  you pull.
+- Stop `rojo serve` before anything that rewrites many files at once: `git checkout`, `switch`,
+  `pull`, `rebase`, `reset`, `stash`, `pesde install`. Restart it afterward.
+- Before pushing, run the checks from the README's Checks section (`rojo sourcemap`,
+  `luau-lsp analyze`, `selene src`, `stylua --check src`) and run the specs in your dev place.
+
+## Keeping `default.project.json` healthy
+
+This file decides where every folder lands in the place. A bad merge here once broke the
+sourcemap and hid the Jest packages from the specs. To keep that from happening again:
+
+- **The README's Layout table is the contract.** If you change a mount, update the table in the
+  same PR. If you resolve a conflict, make the result match the table.
+- **Resolve conflicts by reading both sides, not by taking one.** Keep every mount from both
+  branches, each in its intended place. In particular:
+  - `test_packages/roblox_packages` mounts at `ServerScriptService.Tests.Packages`, never under
+    `ReplicatedStorage`. Jest requires it from there.
+  - `globIgnorePaths` must keep `src/ServerScriptService/Tests`. Without it, the `Tests` folder
+    gets mounted twice.
+  - Check each `$path` against the real folder name (`StarterPlayerScripts`, with the final
+    `s`). Rojo doesn't warn about a path that doesn't exist.
+- **Save it as UTF-8 without a byte order mark.** Rojo reports "Failed to parse JSONC" for a
+  project file that starts with a BOM. Windows PowerShell 5.1's `Set-Content` and `Out-File`
+  add one, and some editors and merge tools do too. Set your editor to plain "UTF-8", not
+  "UTF-8 with BOM".
+- **Verify after any edit or merge:** run
+  `rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts`. It has to
+  succeed, and `ServerScriptService.Tests.Packages.Jest` and
+  `StarterPlayer.StarterPlayerScripts` have to show up in `sourcemap.json`. Then reconnect
+  `rojo serve` and check that the place looks right in Studio's Explorer.
